{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Who [is among you].</b> The prophet speaks with these:" "<b>Who walks in darkness.</b> Return to the one who fears HaShem, who does not seek greatness and the desires of the world, let him trust in HaShem. And some say that \"who walks in darkness\" [return to the one who fears HaShem] describes His servant, who is the prophet, and the meaning is: who is even among you, like \"there is not among you,\" because you see the prophet has no superiority in this world, and this is the correct interpretation because of the verse that follows after it."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 50, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:54.510424642Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}